From: Ivan Semenov <ivan@ray.app>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mxl-gsw1xx: wire 802.1Q tagging ops for GSW150

The 8021q tagging support (910) wires the tag_8021q hw_info hooks for
the GSW12x, GSW140 and GSW141 variants but not for the Intel GSW150
added later. The GL.iNet GL-SFT1200 carries a GSW150, so without these
hooks the dsa,tag-8021q DT property is silently ignored on that board.

Signed-off-by: Ivan Semenov <ivan@ray.app>
---
 drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/mxl-gsw1xx.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/mxl-gsw1xx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/lantiq/mxl-gsw1xx.c
@@ -1018,6 +1018,11 @@ static const struct gswip_hw_info gsw150
 		[6] = 11,
 	},
 	.phylink_get_caps	= gsw150_phylink_get_caps,
+	.get_tag_protocol	= gsw1xx_get_tag_protocol,
+	.change_tag_protocol	= gsw1xx_change_tag_protocol,
+	.tag_8021q_vlan_add	= gsw1xx_tag_8021q_vlan_add,
+	.tag_8021q_vlan_del	= gsw1xx_tag_8021q_vlan_del,
+	.teardown		= gsw1xx_teardown,
 	.pce_microcode		= &gsw1xx_pce_microcode,
 	.pce_microcode_size	= ARRAY_SIZE(gsw1xx_pce_microcode),
 	.tag_protocol		= DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL_GSW1XX,
